turboexl3_ds41 builds against the mlx-serve plugin kit and turboexl3 (build.zig.zon, by URL and hash). It vendors
nothing: the code below came from mlx-serve, which no longer carries it, and is maintained here (no copy to sync).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlx-serve
https://github.com/ddalcu/mlx-serve
Copyright (c) 2026 David Dalcu
Licensed under the MIT License.

src/streamed/ and src/exl3/ are mlx-serve's DeepSeek-V4.1 EXL3 lane (its bank, source and waves, from
src/sdk/weights/streamed/ and src/sdk/quant/exl3/stream/), moved out of mlx-serve into this plugin at ddalcu/mlx-serve
72e87026 with the imports pointed at this plugin's files and the kit, and this plugin's own edits since; the stream
itself is the kit's (`kit.streamed`). src/bank/ (DeepSeek-V4.1's schedule over the stream) is this plugin's own code,
back from mlx-serve, which carried it for a while. src/streamed/sdk/{env,log,shared}.zig and src/host_shims.zig are
this plugin's code standing in for mlx-serve's registry, log, unit globals and C++ shims over MLX's private headers.
The src/*_test.zig gates are this plugin's.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlx-stream
https://github.com/davidtai/mlx-stream
Copyright (c) 2026 David Tai
Licensed under the MIT License.

mlx-serve absorbed mlx-stream (the SSD expert streamer, its SDK and C read pool, and the DeepSeek-V4.1 EXL3 decoder
with its pinned Metal kernels); src/streamed/ and src/exl3/ hold the EXL3 parts, the kit ships the streamer. The streaming runtime they were ported
from (the packed expert record and manifest formats, the streamed-bank layout and the routed-expert EXL3 Metal
kernels) is David Tai's earlier work. It incorporates:
- MLX (https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx, Copyright (c) 2023-2025 Apple Inc., MIT): the kernel texts under
  src/exl3/kernels/exl3/ inline MLX's steel headers, each section marked with its MLX source path and copyright line.
- ExLlamaV3 (https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3, Copyright (c) turboderp, MIT): the EXL3 format it reads
  follows exllamav3 v1.4.2 (codebook.cuh, exl3_dq.cuh, pack.cu, hadamard.cu, quantize.py); src/exl3/{quant,kernels}.zig
  cite the lines they reproduce. No exllamav3 code is shipped.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/fixtures/config.json is the config.json of OpensourceWTF/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-exl3-2.81bpw (the SC 2.81bpw
EXL3 pack of DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash; license MIT, as DeepSeek's release), unchanged.
